Feature scaling - Worked Example.
In this example, we will load a small dataset, apply Min-Max Scaling and Standardization, and compare the results.
We have a dataset of employees with their Age and Salary. Since Salary values are much larger than Age, we will scale the features so that 
both can be compared fairly.

Step 1: Make a tiny dataset

data = {"Age": [...], "Salary": [...]}
df = pd.DataFrame(data)
We build a small table with two columns: Age and Salary.
This shows a common real-world issue: numbers live on very different ranges (Age: tens, Salary: thousands).

Step 2: Min-Max Scaling (0 to 1)

minmax_scaler = MinMaxScaler()
df_minmax = pd.DataFrame(minmax_scaler.fit_transform(df), columns=df.columns)
What it does: squeezes each column so its minimum becomes 0 and maximum becomes 1.
fit_transform does two things:
fit: looks at the column’s min and max.
transform: applies (x - min) / (max - min) to every value.
We wrap the result back into a DataFrame and keep the original column names so it’s easy to read.

Step 3: Standardization (mean 0, std 1)

standard_scaler = StandardScaler()
df_standard = pd.DataFrame(standard_scaler.fit_transform(df), columns=df.columns)
What it does: centers each column to mean = 0 and scales to standard deviation = 1.
Useful when features have different spreads or when you expect outliers.
Again, we use fit_transform and rebuild a labeled DataFrame for readability.
What you should notice

In Min-Max, values are between 0 and 1.
In Standardization, values are centered around 0 (you’ll see negative and positive numbers).
After scaling, Age won’t be overshadowed by Salary just because Salary has larger numbers.

#############################  CODE here #################3

import pandas as pd
from sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler, StandardScaler

# Dataset
data = {
    "Age": [22, 25, 30, 35, 40],
    "Salary": [25000, 40000, 60000, 80000, 100000]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

print("Original Dataset:\n")
print(df)

# Min-Max Scaling
minmax_scaler = MinMaxScaler()

df_minmax = pd.DataFrame(
    minmax_scaler.fit_transform(df),
    columns=df.columns
)

print("\nMin-Max Scaled Dataset:\n")
print(df_minmax)

# Standardization
standard_scaler = StandardScaler()

df_standard = pd.DataFrame(
    standard_scaler.fit_transform(df),
    columns=df.columns
)

print("\nStandardized Dataset:\n")
print(df_standard)

